            "title": "Offensive security: break it on purpose",
            "body": "**Offensive security** simulates real attacks to find vulnerabilities **before** criminals do. Back to the machine: you **hire someone to try to break it**, they find the dispenser gap, and you build a mitigation so it can't be repeated. The main flavours are **penetration testing** (a focused, authorised attempt to breach a defined scope), **vulnerability assessment** (systematically listing weaknesses, often with scanners), and **red teaming** (a stealthy, goal-driven simulation of a real adversary). The deliverable is always a report of findings that defenders can act on.",
