            "title": "Practice set: 5 CIDRs to solve",
            "body": "Solve these by hand, then reveal. For each, give network, broadcast, usable range, and host count. **(1)** `10.0.0.0/8` → ||network 10.0.0.0, broadcast 10.255.255.255, hosts 10.0.0.1–10.255.255.254, 16,777,214 usable (24 host bits).|| **(2)** `172.16.0.0/16` → ||network 172.16.0.0, broadcast 172.16.255.255, hosts 172.16.0.1–172.16.255.254, 65,534 usable.|| **(3)** `192.168.10.0/26` → ||network .0, broadcast .63, hosts .1–.62, 62 usable.|| **(4)** `192.168.10.64/27` → ||network .64, broadcast .95, hosts .65–.94, 30 usable.|| **(5)** `192.168.10.200/29` → ||block size 8, so this falls in the .200 subnet: network .200, broadcast .207, hosts .201–.206, 6 usable.|| Check your work against the formulas before peeking.",
