            "title": "The goal: one script, full snapshot",
            "body": "The objective is a single `.ps1` that answers 'what's running, who exists, and what auto-runs?' — the three questions behind both incident triage and post-exploitation enumeration. We'll use **`Get-Process`** (processes), **`Get-LocalUser`** (accounts), and **`Get-ScheduledTask`** (persistence/automation). Analogy: a doctor's full-vitals sheet instead of three separate check-ups. Worked example skeleton: `Write-Host \"== Processes ==\"; Get-Process | Sort-Object CPU -Descending | Select-Object -First 10`. This top-10-by-CPU view is the scriptable version of Task Manager's Performance tab.",
