            "title": "RBAC: permissions by role",
            "body": "**Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** ties permissions to a predefined **role** — e.g. 'Admin' vs 'User', each with its own permission set. You get access because of the hat you wear, not your individual name. **Analogy:** a hospital — a 'Doctor' badge opens the pharmacy, a 'Visitor' badge does not, regardless of the person. **Worked example:** promoting someone to Manager instantly grants every Manager permission — simple to manage, but coarse. Predict a weakness: ||RBAC is coarse — it can't easily say 'Managers, but only during work hours from the office' without extra attributes (that's ABAC).||",
