        "number": 65,
        "title": "Common Encoding Schemes (Base64, URL encoding, HTML encoding)",
        "type": "theory",
        "week": 5,
        "description": "Encoding schemes exist to safely represent data in a channel that only accepts certain characters - never to hide or protect it. This topic covers the three you'll meet constantly: Base64, URL (percent) encoding, and HTML entity encoding. You'll learn to recognize each by eye and understand why HTML encoding is the core defence against XSS.",
