        "description": "A corporate network is simply all the computers, servers, printers and phones in a company wired together so people can share work and data. Understanding how it is laid out matters because, as an attacker or defender, the structure decides what you can reach once you get a foothold. This lesson builds the office-building mental model you will reuse for every later topic.",
