            "title": "802.1Q tagging and trunks",
            "body": "When many VLANs must travel over a single cable between two switches, that cable is a **trunk link**, and the switches use **802.1Q** — the standard that inserts a small VLAN tag into each Ethernet frame so the far switch knows which room the frame belongs to. Analogy: a mail van carrying letters for every floor, each envelope stamped with its floor number so sorting stays correct at the other end. Access ports (to a single PC) carry one untagged VLAN; trunk ports carry many tagged VLANs.",
