            "body": "Because VLAN separation is enforced by switch config, misconfiguration lets attackers **VLAN-hop** out of their assigned room. Two classic techniques: **switch spoofing**, where the attacker's machine pretends to be a switch and negotiates a trunk (abusing auto-trunking like Cisco DTP) to receive every VLAN's traffic; and **double tagging**, where the attacker wraps a frame in two 802.1Q tags so the first switch strips one and forwards it into a VLAN it should never reach. Predict the fix for switch spoofing: ||Disable auto-trunking (DTP) and hard-set user ports to access mode, not dynamic.||",
