        "description": "A DMZ is a buffer subnet that holds the servers a company must expose to the internet, kept separate from the trusted internal network. It exists so that if a public server is hacked, the attacker is stuck in the buffer instead of inside the company. You need it because reaching the internal network from the DMZ is a classic attacker goal and a classic defensive failure.",
