        "description": "Zero Trust throws out the old idea that everything inside the corporate network can be trusted, and instead verifies every user and device on every request. It matters because attackers routinely get inside the perimeter, so trusting 'the inside' is exactly how one foothold becomes total compromise. This lesson explains the mindset, its principles and the controls that enforce it.",
