            "title": "Anomaly-based detection",
            "body": "**Anomaly-based** detection first learns a **baseline** of what 'normal' traffic looks like, then flags **deviations** from it. Because it keys on *unusual*, not *known-bad*, it can catch **brand-new attacks** a signature system would miss. The trade-off is a **higher false-positive rate** — legitimate-but-unusual activity (a big quarterly backup, a new app) can trip the alarm. Analogy: a bank noticing your card is suddenly used abroad for a huge purchase — the pattern is abnormal for you, even if that exact transaction is on no blacklist.",
