            "body": "A company hardens `www.example.com` carefully — but `dev.example.com`, `old-portal.example.com`, or `vpn.example.com` are often forgotten, running older software with weaker controls. Attackers love subdomains because they **expand the attack surface** far beyond the main domain and tend to hide the weakest link. Analogy: the front door of a mansion is reinforced, but the gardener's side gate was installed years ago and never upgraded. Finding every subdomain is therefore one of the highest-value recon activities.",
