            "body": "**Data exfiltration** is extracting data out of the target environment — the usual end goal of a real attack. Attackers often use **covert channels** to blend the theft into normal traffic: tunneling data over DNS queries, hiding it in HTTPS to a cloud service, or trickling it out slowly to avoid volume alerts. Analogy: smuggling documents out a few pages at a time inside ordinary-looking mail. In an authorized test you only move the *minimum* data needed to prove impact — never real customer data beyond PoC need, per the engagement's hard limits.",
