            "title": "Two ways to feed Burp traffic",
            "body": "You have two choices. The easy one: Burp ships its **own embedded Chromium browser** (Proxy > Intercept > Open Browser) already wired to intercept — nothing to configure. The flexible one: route **your everyday browser** (we use **Firefox**) through Burp using the **FoxyProxy** extension, so you can flip interception on and off with one click and keep your normal bookmarks and logins. We set up Firefox once; it stays configured for the whole course. The embedded browser is a pre-tuned rental car; your own browser + FoxyProxy is tuning your own car once so it's always ready.",
