            "title": "Point Firefox at Burp with FoxyProxy",
            "body": "**FoxyProxy** is a Firefox extension that switches proxy settings on and off without digging through menus. Steps: install FoxyProxy from the add-ons store, open its **proxy configuration**, add a new proxy entry, and set **hostname = `127.0.0.1`** and **port = `8080`** — matching Burp's listener exactly. Name it 'Burp.' FoxyProxy is a light switch you wire once; after that one flip sends Firefox's traffic down the Burp hallway. A common mistake is a port typo — predict what happens if you set `8081` instead. ||Firefox tries to reach a proxy that isn't there, so pages fail to load until you fix the port back to `8080`.||",
