            "title": "Who OWASP is and what the list is",
            "body": "**OWASP** (the Open Worldwide Application Security Project) is a non-profit that publishes free security resources — no logins, no paywall. Its most famous one is the **OWASP Top 10**: a short awareness document naming the ten most critical categories of web-application risk. Think of it like a hospital's list of the ten most common causes of admission — it does not describe every illness, but it tells a new doctor what to rule out first. It is refreshed about every four years; the edition everyone uses today is **2021**.",
