            "title": "Categories, not individual bugs",
            "body": "A common beginner mistake is thinking the Top 10 lists specific bugs. It does not. Each entry is a **category** — a family of related weaknesses. For example **A03: Injection** is not one bug; it is an umbrella covering SQL injection, cross-site scripting, OS command injection and more, all of which share the same root cause: the app mistaking attacker input for code. The analogy: 'vehicle collisions' is a category, while 'rear-ended at the Main Street light on Tuesday' is a specific incident. Question: is `SQL injection` its own Top 10 entry? ||No — it lives inside the broader A03: Injection category, alongside XSS and command injection.||",
