            "title": "The shell operators you will use",
            "body": "Four operators chain commands, each with different logic. `;` runs the next command **regardless** of whether the first succeeded or failed. `&&` runs the next command **only if** the first *succeeded* (exit code 0). `||` runs the next **only if** the first *failed*. `|` (pipe) feeds the **output** of the first command as input to the second. Separately, redirection (`>`, `>>`, `<`) writes or reads files. Analogy: `;` is 'do this, then that, no matter what'; `&&` is 'do this, and only if it works, do that'; `|` is 'take what this produced and hand it to the next worker'. Knowing which to inject matters when the first command might error out.",
