        "title": "CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery)",
        "type": "theory",
        "week": 9,
        "description": "CSRF tricks a victim's browser into sending a state-changing request to a site they are already logged into, by abusing the fact that browsers automatically attach that site's cookies to every request — no matter which page triggered it. The attacker never sees the response or the cookie; they just get the victim to load a page that silently fires the request as the victim. It matters because it can change a victim's email or password, or transfer their funds, without ever stealing a credential.",
