        "week": 10,
        "description": "SSTI happens when an app builds a page by pasting your input straight into a template that the server then compiles and runs, instead of passing your input to the template as plain data. A probe as innocent as `{{7*7}}` returning `49` proves the server is executing your text as code. It matters because most template engines expose a path from that trick to full remote code execution.",
