            "title": "Data versus code: the core mistake",
            "body": "A template engine fills blanks in a page: the template `Hello {{ name }}` plus data `name='Dan'` renders `Hello Dan`. That is safe — your value is **data** dropped into a blank. SSTI appears when a developer builds the template string *itself* out of your input, e.g. Flask's `render_template_string(f'Hello {name}!')`. Now your input is part of the **template source**, so the engine compiles and executes it. Think of a form letter: safe apps write your name in the blank; a vulnerable one lets you rewrite the letter's instructions.",
