            "title": "Jinja2 to RCE: walking the object graph",
            "body": "In Python's Jinja2 you rarely call `os` directly — the sandbox hides it — so you walk the object graph to reach it. A reliable chain: `{{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('whoami').read()}}` climbs from an exposed object up to its module globals, grabs the `os` module, and runs `popen`. Another classic uses `''.__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__()` to enumerate every loaded class and find one that spawns processes. The lesson: SSTI in a 'sandboxed' engine is still RCE, because the language's own introspection bridges back to the operating system.",
