            "title": "Mass assignment",
            "body": "**Mass assignment** happens when an endpoint copies *every* field you send straight into the record. Code like `User.findByIdAndUpdate(req.user.id, req.body)` binds the whole request body to the model. The profile form only shows name and email, but you add `\"role\":\"admin\"` (or `\"isVerified\":true`, `\"balance\":99999`) to the JSON and the server writes it — privilege escalation with no 'make me admin' button anywhere. The fix is an **allowlist** of updatable fields (bind only `name` and `email`), never blindly binding `req.body`.",
