            "title": "Find the hidden surface first",
            "body": "You cannot attack endpoints you cannot see, so enumerate them. Proxy the app's own traffic to learn its real requests, then look for a **machine-readable spec**: `/openapi.json`, `/swagger`, `/swagger-ui`, `/api-docs`, or a bare `/api`. These often list every endpoint, method, and parameter — including ones the UI never calls. For GraphQL, **introspection** dumps the full schema the same way. The spec is a map of the whole attack surface, frequently exposing admin or debug routes the front-end hides.",
