            "body": "In a PortSwigger API lab, the app sends `PATCH /api/user/wiener` to update a profile. Trim the path down to `PATCH /api` and the server returns interactive **API documentation** that was never linked in the UI. That documentation exposes a hidden **DELETE** method on the user endpoint — not offered anywhere on the site. Using it, you send `DELETE /api/user/carlos` and remove another user. The lesson: probing parent paths and malformed routes can reveal undocumented, more powerful methods than the UI admits.",
