            "title": "Other API failures and defences",
            "body": "Beyond BOLA and mass assignment: **unauthenticated admin routes** like `/api/admin/users` that forgot an auth check; **server-side parameter pollution** by sending a parameter twice (`?category=public&category=private`) to confuse backend parsing; and **SSRF** via an endpoint that fetches an attacker-supplied `url`. Defend across the board: enforce **object-level authorization on every request** (check ownership, not just login); **allowlist** bindable fields to kill mass assignment; require auth on *all* routes including admin and docs; and validate/allowlist any URL or repeated parameter the API accepts.",
