        "description": "A guided walkthrough of PortSwigger's 'web shell upload via path traversal' lab. The avatar endpoint stores PHP uploads but will not execute them from that folder, so you rename the upload with a URL-encoded traversal to escape into a folder where PHP runs, then read a secret file. It makes the upload-bypass theory concrete end to end.",
