            "title": "The Windows privilege ladder",
            "body": "Windows has a hierarchy: a **standard user**, then **Administrator**, then **SYSTEM**, the built-in account the OS itself runs as, with even more power over the machine than an admin. Privesc on Windows means climbing this ladder, typically from a standard user toward SYSTEM. As on Linux, the usual route is **misconfiguration**: a sloppy service, a permissive installer policy, or abusable privileges. Analogy: SYSTEM is the building's master key held by the facilities system itself, more than any human manager's key.",
