            "title": "AlwaysInstallElevated",
            "body": "**AlwaysInstallElevated** is a Windows policy that, when enabled, lets *any* user install an **MSI package with SYSTEM privileges**. It's meant to help non-admins install approved software, but if both required registry keys are set (under HKCU and HKLM), an attacker simply crafts a malicious MSI and installs it to run code as SYSTEM. Check it by querying those registry values; if both are `1`, you craft an MSI (e.g. with msfvenom) that spawns a shell and run `msiexec` to install it. It's a single misconfiguration that hands you SYSTEM outright.",
