            "body": "While a run proceeds, Hashcat prints a live **status block**. Watch **Recovered** (hashes cracked so far out of total), **Progress** (how far through the keyspace/wordlist), and **Speed** in **kH/s** (throughput). These tell you whether you're nearly done or barely started. The reference run cracked an unsalted hash in **well under a second at ~72,253 kH/s**, a single weak, unsalted hash against rockyou.txt is often near-instant. If Speed is tiny, suspect you're on CPU-only (VM without GPU).",
