        "type": "theory",
        "week": 11,
        "description": "Every network tool you write either speaks the raw language of the network (sockets) or a polite higher-level protocol like HTTP (requests). This topic teaches both layers from scratch so you understand what actually happens when your script 'connects' to a target. Get these two libraries right and you can build a port scanner, a subdomain checker, and a login brute-forcer.",
