            "body": "A good tool **confirms** its own work rather than assuming success. The command succeeding (exit code 0) does not prove the MAC actually changed — so after running the three commands, the script re-reads the interface with `subprocess.check_output([\"ip\",\"link\",\"show\",iface])` and uses a regex to **extract the live MAC** from that output. It then compares the live MAC against the one you requested. Analogy: after mailing a letter you **check the mailbox flag is down** rather than assuming the carrier took it. Predict: why not just trust the exit code of `ip link`? ||Because the command can succeed while the driver quietly refuses or resets the address — only reading back the live MAC proves the change truly stuck.||",
