            "title": "What credential brute-forcing is",
            "body": "**Brute-forcing** a login means automatically trying many **username/password combinations** until one works, exploiting weak or reused passwords. It is the automated version of guessing, powered by **wordlists** of passwords leaked from past breaches — so it isn't random, it tries the passwords real people actually use. Analogy: it's a **thief with a ring of the 200 most common keys**, trying each in the lock far faster than any human. This technique works depressingly often because people pick `password123` and reuse it everywhere. You build this to understand the attack well enough to defend against it — and to test login pages you're authorised to assess.",
