            "title": "What AI flags well",
            "body": "AI review is strong on common, pattern-based vulnerabilities: **SQL Injection** (user input bent into a database query), **Cross-Site Scripting / XSS** (injected malicious scripts in a page), **Buffer Overflow** (writing past a memory limit to crash or hijack a program), and **hardcoded passwords** stored right in the source. Analogy: a metal detector is great at finding the common metals it's tuned for. Worked example: it spots `query = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='\" + input + \"'\"` as a textbook SQL-injection pattern instantly.",
