            "title": "The toolkit",
            "body": "Four tools, each with a role: **GitHub Copilot** gives inline suggestions and warns about bad practices as you type; **CodeQL** is static analysis that matches your code against known vulnerability patterns (you query code like a database); **Semgrep** is lightweight, customisable rule-based scanning; and **ChatGPT/LLMs** explain and review code conversationally. Analogy: Copilot is the spell-checker underlining as you write; CodeQL and Semgrep are the dedicated editors doing a full pass; ChatGPT is the colleague you ask 'is this safe?'.",
