            "title": "The platforms",
            "body": "Most programs are hosted on **platforms** that act as the middleman between researchers and companies. The two largest are **HackerOne** and **Bugcrowd**; others include **Intigriti** and **YesWeHack**. The platform handles the program rules, your report submission, communication, triage and payment, so you do not negotiate directly with the company's lawyers. Think of them as the freelance marketplace (like a job board) connecting hackers to companies that want testing. You create one account, then opt into individual programs, each with its own rules and rewards.",
