            "title": "Scope and safe harbor — the rules that keep you legal",
            "body": "Before touching anything you must read the program's **scope**: the explicit list of domains, apps and IPs you *are* allowed to test, and an **out-of-scope** list you must *never* touch. Equally vital is the **safe harbor** clause — a promise the company will not pursue legal action *as long as you follow the rules*. Analogy: scope is the fenced area of the test range; step outside the fence and the safe harbor protection evaporates, turning your 'research' into illegal intrusion. Golden rule: **in scope and in the rules = protected; one step outside = potential crime.** No bug, however impressive, is worth testing out of scope.",
