            "title": "What a CTF is",
            "body": "A **Capture The Flag (CTF)** is a hacking competition where each challenge hides a secret string — the **flag**, usually formatted like `flag{y0u_found_me}` — somewhere you can only reach by exploiting a weakness. You submit the flag to score points. Analogy: an escape room for hackers, where finding the hidden key proves you solved the puzzle. Everything is intentionally vulnerable and you are *meant* to attack it, so it is completely legal and safe. The roadmap names CTF practice as the **first hands-on activity** in the whole journey, next to networking basics and the CIA triad.",
