        "description": "DCSync is one of the most damaging AD attacks: instead of hacking a domain controller, you politely ask it to replicate password data to you, and it obliges because it believes you are another DC. With the right replication permissions — often obtained by abusing a misconfigured ACL — an attacker pulls every hash in the domain, including krbtgt. This topic explains the protocol, the rights, the tools, and why it blends into normal traffic.",
