            "title": "SharpHound + BloodHound — the attack-path map",
            "body": "**SharpHound** is the **collector** (a C# binary, or `Invoke-BloodHound`); it walks AD over **LDAP** and enumerates **sessions** over SMB/RPC, then dumps **JSON**. **BloodHound** ingests that JSON and draws a **graph** of users, groups, machines, and the **edges** between them (AdminTo, MemberOf, GenericAll, CanRDP...). Its killer feature: the **\"Shortest Paths to Domain Admins\"** query, which literally **draws the attack chain** for you. Analogy: instead of a flashlight, a full lit-up blueprint showing every corridor from the lobby to the vault. This is the same graph the L16 lab has you read edge by edge.",
