        "title": "Windows Privesc Enumeration Methodology",
        "type": "theory",
        "week": 14,
        "description": "You have just landed a low-privilege shell on a Windows box and you have no idea which of a dozen possible misconfigurations will hand you SYSTEM. Enumeration is the disciplined checklist that answers that question before you waste time on exploits that can't work here. Learning the manual checklist first is what lets you keep going when your automated tool gets flagged by antivirus or can't be uploaded.",
