            "title": "What works and what does not through proxychains",
            "body": "A critical limitation: proxychains can only wrap standard socket **`connect()`** calls, not raw packet crafting. So nmap **TCP connect scans (`-sT`) work**, but **SYN scans (`-sS`) generally do not**, because `-sS` crafts raw packets that bypass the socket layer proxychains hooks. Same reason ICMP ping and some UDP tricks fail. Rule of thumb through a pivot: use `-sT -Pn` for nmap, and prefer tools that make ordinary TCP connections. Predict: your `proxychains nmap -sS 10.0.0.5` returns nothing useful, why? ||-sS uses raw SYN packets that proxychains cannot intercept; switch to -sT, which uses connect().||",
