        "type": "theory",
        "week": 15,
        "description": "WEP was WiFi's original encryption, and it is studied today mainly as a cautionary tale of how a scheme can be broken by design rather than by misuse. Understanding exactly why WEP fails — a short, reused, cleartext number called the IV — is what makes the smarter design of WPA/WPA2 make sense.",
