            "body": "Because the PMK and PTK are never transmitted, there is no math that turns a captured handshake back into the passphrase. The only way forward is to **guess a candidate passphrase**, run it through the same chain — PSK -> PBKDF2 -> PMK -> PTK -> MIC — and compare the resulting MIC to the captured one. A match means that guess is the real passphrase. Worked example: guess `summer2024`, derive its MIC, compare to the capture; no match means try the next candidate, forever, until the list runs out. This is **offline**: once you have the capture you need no further contact with the network, so there is no lockout or rate limit to slow you down.",
