            "title": "A different kind of attack: target the person",
            "body": "Cracking handshakes and WPS PINs all attacked the *math* of authentication. The **Evil Twin** attack sidesteps the math entirely and attacks the *person*. Instead of breaking encryption, the attacker makes a convincing fake of a trusted network and lets the victim hand over credentials willingly. Analogy: rather than picking a bank's lock, a con artist sets up a fake bank branch and waits for customers to walk in and deposit their money. This is a mindset shift worth pausing on: when the technology is strong, attackers pivot to the humans using it. That makes Evil Twin fundamentally a deception technique, not a cryptographic one.",
