            "title": "Tools that automate it",
            "body": "Setting up the rogue AP, running the deauth, and serving the captive portal by hand would be fiddly, so tools like **airgeddon** and **wifiphisher** bundle the whole workflow into an integrated, menu-driven process. They spin up the fake AP, handle the deauth of the real one, host the phishing portal, and collect whatever the victim submits. Analogy: a ready-made con-artist kit — the fake storefront, the distraction, and the fraudulent forms all in one box. Knowing these tools exist matters for defenders too: the barrier to running this attack is low, so it is a realistic threat on any open or guest network, not just a lab curiosity.",
