        "week": 16,
        "description": "Every EC2 server can quietly ask a hidden internal address about itself — including, dangerously, the temporary keys for whatever permissions that server holds. If an attacker can trick a vulnerable app into asking that address on their behalf, a minor web bug turns into a full cloud-account compromise. This chain, SSRF into the metadata service, is one of the most impactful techniques in cloud attacks.",
