            "title": "No logs, no incident response",
            "body": "The consequence of a logging gap is severe: with no CloudTrail history, incident responders **cannot reconstruct** what happened, when it started, or how far the intrusion spread. Worked example: a company discovers a breach but CloudTrail was off for the critical window — they can't tell which data was accessed, so they must assume the worst and notify every customer. Logging gaps directly limit response capability and turn a contained incident into an open-ended one.",
